      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that the charge has to be in the old mm\u0027s units: `MM_ANONPAGES` of a 4KB mm counts 4KB pages, which is also what `oom_badness()` assumes since aosp/4312502.\n\nIt looks like `mm_reader_pages()` (aosp/4366897, in `include/linux/p3s/mm.h`) already does this conversion: it scales a page count of an mm to the page size of `current`, rounding up, and its stub returns the count unchanged. Its kernel-doc talks about /proc readers, but the math is the same, and `current-\u003emm` is the old mm here. Would converting in `get_arg_page()` work for you? Something like:\n\n```\n\tif (write)\n\t\tacct_arg_size(bprm, mm_reader_pages(mm, vma_pages(vma)));\n```\n\n`mm` is `bprm-\u003emm` there. `bprm-\u003evma_pages` then holds the charge in the old mm\u0027s pages, which is what `acct_arg_size(bprm, 0)` takes back, and `acct_arg_size()` keeps upstream\u0027s code, including the `!mm || !diff` early return.",
